enable justIntonation;

use "@std"
use "@audio"
use "@composition"

Note: ============================================================
Note:  Pragma demo: enable justIntonation; -- 5-limit Just Intonation
Note: ============================================================

(print "Flow Pragma Demo -- enable justIntonation;")
(print "Generating examples/output/microtonal_ji.{wav,mid} ...")

Note: With `enable justIntonation;` at line 1, the C-major triad renders with
Note: PURE just-intonation ratios:
Note:   C-E (major third) -> ratio 5/4 = 1.25       (12-TET ~1.2599)
Note:   C-G (perfect fifth) -> ratio 3/2 = 1.5      (12-TET ~1.4983)
Note: The audible difference is the major third -- JI sounds "pure", 12-TET sounds "narrow".

(print "JI major third (C-E):  ratio 5/4 = 1.25")
(print "12-TET major third:    ratio 2^(4/12) ~ 1.2599")
(print "JI fifth (C-G):        ratio 3/2 = 1.5")
(print "12-TET fifth:          ratio 2^(7/12) ~ 1.4983")

Note: Render a Cmaj triad arpeggio + sustained chord under JI.
tempo 120 {
    timesig 4/4 {
        key Cmajor {
            section ji_triad {
                Sequence arp = | C4q E4q G4q C5q |
                Sequence held = | [C4 E4 G4 C5]w |
            }
            Song song = [ji_triad]
            Buffer audio = (renderSong song "piano")
            (writeWav "examples/output/microtonal_ji.wav" audio)
            (writeMidi "examples/output/microtonal_ji.mid" song)
        }
    }
}
(print "WAV:  examples/output/microtonal_ji.wav")
(print "MIDI: examples/output/microtonal_ji.mid")
(print "JI Cmaj triad rendered -- major third at 5:4 ratio")
